2.5.4 Installing MySQL on Linux Using RPM Packages from Oracle
--------------------------------------------------------------

The recommended way to install MySQL on RPM-based Linux distributions is
by using the RPM packages provided by Oracle.  There are two sources for
obtaining them, for the Community Edition of MySQL:

   * From the MySQL software repositories:

        * The MySQL Yum repository (see *note
          linux-installation-yum-repo:: for details).

        * The MySQL SLES repository (see *note
