6.8.1 lz4_decompress -- Decompress mysqlpump LZ4-Compressed Output
------------------------------------------------------------------

The *note 'lz4_decompress': lz4-decompress. utility decompresses *note
'mysqlpump': mysqlpump. output that was created using LZ4 compression.

*Note*:

*note 'lz4_decompress': lz4-decompress. is deprecated as of MySQL
8.0.34; expect it to be removed in a future version of MySQL. This is
because the associated *note 'mysqlpump': mysqlpump. utility is
deprecated as of MySQL 8.0.34.

*Note*:

If MySQL was configured with the '-DWITH_LZ4=system' option, *note
'lz4_decompress': lz4-decompress. is not built.  In this case, the
system 'lz4' command can be used instead.

Invoke *note 'lz4_decompress': lz4-decompress. like this:

     lz4_decompress INPUT_FILE OUTPUT_FILE

Example:

     mysqlpump --compress-output=LZ4 > dump.lz4
     lz4_decompress dump.lz4 dump.txt

To see a help message, invoke *note 'lz4_decompress': lz4-decompress.
with no arguments.

To decompress *note 'mysqlpump': mysqlpump. ZLIB-compressed output, use
*note 'zlib_decompress': zlib-decompress.  See *note zlib-decompress::.


