     more information, see *note server-configuration-validation::.

   * '--validate-user-plugins[={OFF|ON}]'

     Command-Line Format

     '--validate-user-plugins[={OFF|ON}]'

     Type

     Boolean

     Default Value

     'ON'

     If this option is enabled (the default), the server checks each
     user account and produces a warning if conditions are found that
     would make the account unusable:

        * The account requires an authentication plugin that is not
          loaded.

        * The account requires the 'sha256_password' or
          'caching_sha2_password' authentication plugin but the server
          was started with neither SSL nor RSA enabled as required by
          the plugin.

     Enabling '--validate-user-plugins' slows down server initialization
     and 'FLUSH PRIVILEGES'.  If you do not require the additional
     checking, you can disable this option at startup to avoid the
     performance decrement.

   * '--verbose', '-v'

     Use this option with the '--help' option for detailed help.

   * '--version', '-V'

     Display version information and exit.


