7.6.8 The Keyring Proxy Bridge Plugin
-------------------------------------

MySQL Keyring originally implemented keystore capabilities using server
plugins, but began transitioning to use the component infrastructure in
MySQL 8.0.24.  The transition includes revising the underlying
implementation of keyring plugins to use the component infrastructure.
This is facilitated using the plugin named 'daemon_keyring_proxy_plugin'
that acts as a bridge between the plugin and component service APIs, and
enables keyring plugins to continue to be used with no change to
user-visible characteristics.

'daemon_keyring_proxy_plugin' is built in and nothing need be done to
install or enable it.


