8.3.3 Creating SSL and RSA Certificates and Keys
------------------------------------------------

* Menu:

* creating-ssl-rsa-files-using-mysql::  Creating SSL and RSA Certificates and Keys using MySQL
* creating-ssl-files-using-openssl::  Creating SSL Certificates and Keys Using openssl
* creating-rsa-files-using-openssl::  Creating RSA Keys Using openssl

The following discussion describes how to create the files required for
SSL and RSA support in MySQL. File creation can be performed using
facilities provided by MySQL itself, or by invoking the 'openssl'
command directly.

SSL certificate and key files enable MySQL to support encrypted
connections using SSL. See *note using-encrypted-connections::.

RSA key files enable MySQL to support secure password exchange over
unencrypted connections for accounts authenticated by the
'sha256_password' or 'caching_sha2_password' plugin.  See *note
sha256-pluggable-authentication::, and *note
caching-sha2-pluggable-authentication::.


