8.7.5 SELinux TCP Port Context
------------------------------

* Menu:

* selinux-context-mysqld-tcp-port::  Setting the TCP Port Context for mysqld
* selinux-context-mysql-feature-ports::  Setting the TCP Port Context for MySQL Features

The instructions that follow use the 'semanage' binary to manage port
context; on RHEL, it's part of the 'policycoreutils-python-utils'
package:

     yum install -y policycoreutils-python-utils

After installing the 'semanage' binary, you can list ports defined with
the 'mysqld_port_t' context using 'semanage' with the 'port' option.

     $> semanage port -l | grep mysqld
     mysqld_port_t                  tcp      1186, 3306, 63132-63164


