10.15.5 Tracing Memory Usage
----------------------------

Each stored trace is a string, which is extended (using 'realloc()') as
optimization progresses by appending more data to it.  The
'optimizer_trace_max_mem_size' server system variable sets a limit on
the total amount of memory used by all traces currently being stored.
If this limit is reached, the current trace is not extended, which means
the trace is incomplete; in this case the
'MISSING_BYTES_BEYOND_MAX_MEM_SIZE' column shows the number of bytes
missing from the trace.


