10.15.13 Displaying Traces in Other Applications
------------------------------------------------

Examining a trace in the *note 'mysql': mysql. command-line client can
be made less difficult using the 'pager less' command (or your operating
platform's equivalent).  An alternative can be to send the trace to a
file, similarly to what is shown here:

     SELECT TRACE INTO DUMPFILE FILE
     FROM INFORMATION_SCHEMA.OPTIMIZER_TRACE;

You can then pass this file to a JSON-aware text editor or other viewer,
such as the JsonView add-on for Firefox and Chrome
(https://jsonview.com/), which shows objects in color and allows objects
to be expanded or collapsed.

'INTO DUMPFILE' is preferable to 'INTO OUTFILE' for this purpose, since
the latter escapes newlines.  As noted previously, you should ensure
that 'end_markers_in_json' is 'OFF'when executing the 'SELECT INTO'
statement, so that the output is valid JSON.


