13.4.8 Fetching Spatial Data
----------------------------

Geometry values stored in a table can be fetched in internal format.
You can also convert them to WKT or WKB format.

   * Fetching spatial data in internal format:

     Fetching geometry values using internal format can be useful in
     table-to-table transfers:

          CREATE TABLE geom2 (g GEOMETRY) SELECT g FROM geom;

   * Fetching spatial data in WKT format:

     The 'ST_AsText()' function converts a geometry from internal format
     to a WKT string.

          SELECT ST_AsText(g) FROM geom;

   * Fetching spatial data in WKB format:

     The 'ST_AsBinary()' function converts a geometry from internal
     format to a *note 'BLOB': blob. containing the WKB value.

          SELECT ST_AsBinary(g) FROM geom;


