15.6.7.8 Condition Handling and OUT or INOUT Parameters
.......................................................

If a stored procedure exits with an unhandled exception, modified values
of 'OUT' and 'INOUT' parameters are not propagated back to the caller.

If an exception is handled by a 'CONTINUE' or 'EXIT' handler that
contains a *note 'RESIGNAL': resignal. statement, execution of *note
'RESIGNAL': resignal. pops the Diagnostics Area stack, thus signalling
the exception (that is, the information that existed before entry into
the handler).  If the exception is an error, the values of 'OUT' and
'INOUT' parameters are not propagated back to the caller.


