15.7.7.35 SHOW REPLICA STATUS Statement
.......................................

     SHOW {REPLICA | SLAVE} STATUS [FOR CHANNEL CHANNEL]

This statement provides status information on essential parameters of
the replica threads.  From MySQL 8.0.22, use *note 'SHOW REPLICA
STATUS': show-replica-status. in place of *note 'SHOW SLAVE STATUS':
show-slave-status, which is deprecated from that release.  In releases
before MySQL 8.0.22, use *note 'SHOW SLAVE STATUS': show-slave-status.
The statement requires the 'REPLICATION CLIENT' privilege (or the
deprecated 'SUPER' privilege).

'SHOW REPLICA STATUS' is nonblocking.  When run concurrently with *note
'STOP REPLICA': stop-replica, 'SHOW REPLICA STATUS' returns without
waiting for *note 'STOP REPLICA': stop-replica. to finish shutting down
the replication SQL (applier) thread or replication I/O (receiver)
thread (or both).  This permits use in monitoring and other applications
where getting an immediate response from 'SHOW REPLICA STATUS' is more
important than ensuring that it returned the latest data.  The SLAVE
keyword was replaced with REPLICA in MySQL 8.0.22.

If you issue this statement using the *note 'mysql': mysql. client, you
can use a '\G' statement terminator rather than a semicolon to obtain a
more readable vertical layout:

     mysql> SHOW REPLICA STATUS\G
