15.7.8.1 BINLOG Statement
.........................

     BINLOG 'STR'

*note 'BINLOG': binlog. is an internal-use statement.  It is generated
by the *note 'mysqlbinlog': mysqlbinlog. program as the printable
representation of certain events in binary log files.  (See *note
mysqlbinlog::.)  The ''STR'' value is a base 64-encoded string the that
server decodes to determine the data change indicated by the
corresponding event.

To execute *note 'BINLOG': binlog. statements when applying *note
'mysqlbinlog': mysqlbinlog. output, a user account requires the
'BINLOG_ADMIN' privilege (or the deprecated 'SUPER' privilege), or the
'REPLICATION_APPLIER' privilege plus the appropriate privileges to
execute each log event.

This statement can execute only format description events and row
events.


