17.9.1 InnoDB Table Compression
-------------------------------

* Menu:

* innodb-compression-background::  Overview of Table Compression
* innodb-compression-usage::     Creating Compressed Tables
* innodb-compression-tuning::    Tuning Compression for InnoDB Tables
* innodb-compression-tuning-monitoring::  Monitoring InnoDB Table Compression at Runtime
* innodb-compression-internals::  How Compression Works for InnoDB Tables
* innodb-performance-compression-oltp::  Compression for OLTP Workloads
* innodb-compression-syntax-warnings::  SQL Compression Syntax Warnings and Errors

This section describes 'InnoDB' table compression, which is supported
with 'InnoDB' tables that reside in file_per_table tablespaces or
general tablespaces.  Table compression is enabled using the
'ROW_FORMAT=COMPRESSED' attribute with *note 'CREATE TABLE':
create-table. or *note 'ALTER TABLE': alter-table.


