     Defines the size of the mutex/lock wait array.  Increasing the
     value splits the internal data structure used to coordinate
     threads, for higher concurrency in workloads with large numbers of
     waiting threads.  This setting must be configured when the MySQL
     instance is starting up, and cannot be changed afterward.
     Increasing the value is recommended for workloads that frequently
     produce a large number of waiting threads, typically greater than
     768.

