19.1.5.5 Starting Multi-Source Replicas
.......................................

Once you have added channels for all of the replication sources, issue a
*note 'START REPLICA': start-replica. (or before MySQL 8.0.22, *note
'START SLAVE': start-slave.) statement to start replication.  When you
have enabled multiple channels on a replica, you can choose to either
start all channels, or select a specific channel to start.  For example,
to start the two channels separately, use the *note 'mysql': mysql.
client to issue the following statements:

     mysql> START SLAVE FOR CHANNEL "source_1";
     mysql> START SLAVE FOR CHANNEL "source_2";
     Or from MySQL 8.0.22:
     mysql> START REPLICA FOR CHANNEL "source_1";
     mysql> START REPLICA FOR CHANNEL "source_2";

For the full syntax of the *note 'START REPLICA': start-replica. command
and other available options, see *note start-replica::.

To verify that both channels have started and are operating correctly,
you can issue *note 'SHOW REPLICA STATUS': show-replica-status.
statements on the replica, for example:

     mysql> SHOW SLAVE STATUS FOR CHANNEL "source_1"\G
     mysql> SHOW SLAVE STATUS FOR CHANNEL "source_2"\G
     Or from MySQL 8.0.22:
     mysql> SHOW REPLICA STATUS FOR CHANNEL "source_1"\G
     mysql> SHOW REPLICA STATUS FOR CHANNEL "source_2"\G


