19.1.5.6 Stopping Multi-Source Replicas
.......................................

The *note 'STOP REPLICA': stop-replica. statement can be used to stop a
multi-source replica.  By default, if you use the *note 'STOP REPLICA':
stop-replica. statement on a multi-source replica all channels are
stopped.  Optionally, use the 'FOR CHANNEL CHANNEL' clause to stop only
a specific channel.

   * To stop all currently configured replication channels:

          mysql> STOP SLAVE;
          Or from MySQL 8.0.22:
          mysql> STOP REPLICA;

   * To stop only a named channel, use a 'FOR CHANNEL CHANNEL' clause:

          mysql> STOP SLAVE FOR CHANNEL "source_1";
          Or from MySQL 8.0.22:
          mysql> STOP REPLICA FOR CHANNEL "source_1";

For the full syntax of the *note 'STOP REPLICA': stop-replica. command
and other available options, see *note stop-replica::.


File: manual.info.tmp,  Node: replication-multi-source-reset-replica,  Next: replication-multi-source-monitoring,  Prev: replication-multi-source-stop-replica,  Up: replication-multi-source

19.1.5.7 Resetting Multi-Source Replicas
........................................

The *note 'RESET REPLICA': reset-replica. statement can be used to reset
a multi-source replica.  By default, if you use the *note 'RESET
REPLICA': reset-replica. statement on a multi-source replica all
channels are reset.  Optionally, use the 'FOR CHANNEL CHANNEL' clause to
reset only a specific channel.

   * To reset all currently configured replication channels:

          mysql> RESET SLAVE;
          Or from MySQL 8.0.22:
          mysql> RESET REPLICA;

   * To reset only a named channel, use a 'FOR CHANNEL CHANNEL' clause:

          mysql> RESET SLAVE FOR CHANNEL "source_1";
          Or from MySQL 8.0.22:
          mysql> RESET REPLICA FOR CHANNEL "source_1";

For GTID-based replication, note that *note 'RESET REPLICA':
reset-replica. has no effect on the replica's GTID execution history.
If you want to clear this, issue *note 'RESET MASTER': reset-master. on
the replica.

*note 'RESET REPLICA': reset-replica. makes the replica forget its
replication position, and clears the relay log, but it does not change
any replication connection parameters (such as the source host name) or
replication filters.  If you want to remove these for a channel, issue
*note 'RESET REPLICA ALL': reset-replica.

For the full syntax of the 'RESET REPLICA' command and other available
options, see *note reset-replica::.


