     Unit

     bytes

     Block Size

     '4096'

     If a write by a replica to its relay log causes the current log
     file size to exceed the value of this variable, the replica rotates
     the relay logs (closes the current file and opens the next one).
     If 'max_relay_log_size' is 0, the server uses 'max_binlog_size' for
     both the binary log and the relay log.  If 'max_relay_log_size' is
     greater than 0, it constrains the size of the relay log, which
     enables you to have different sizes for the two logs.  You must set
