20.2.1 Deploying Group Replication in Single-Primary Mode
---------------------------------------------------------

* Menu:

* group-replication-deploying-instances::  Deploying Instances for Group Replication
* group-replication-configuring-instances::  Configuring an Instance for Group Replication
* group-replication-user-credentials::  User Credentials For Distributed Recovery
* group-replication-launching::  Launching Group Replication
* group-replication-bootstrap::  Bootstrapping the Group
* group-replication-adding-instances::  Adding Instances to the Group

Each of the MySQL server instances in a group can run on an independent
physical host machine, which is the recommended way to deploy Group
Replication.  This section explains how to create a replication group
with three MySQL Server instances, each running on a different host
machine.  See *note group-replication-deploying-locally:: for
information about deploying multiple MySQL server instances running
Group Replication on the same host machine, for example for testing
purposes.

FIGURE GOES HERE: Group Architecture

This tutorial explains how to get and deploy MySQL Server with the Group
Replication plugin, how to configure each server instance before
creating a group, and how to use Performance Schema monitoring to verify
that everything is working correctly.


