22.4 Python Quick-Start Guide: MySQL Shell for Document Store
=============================================================

* Menu:

* mysql-shell-tutorial-python-shell::  MySQL Shell
* mysql-shell-tutorial-python-download::  Download and Import world_x Database
* mysql-shell-tutorial-python-documents-collections::  Documents and Collections
* mysql-shell-tutorial-python-relational-tables::  Relational Tables
* mysql-shell-tutorial-python-documents-in-tables::  Documents in Tables

This quick-start guide provides instructions to begin prototyping
document store applications interactively with MySQL Shell.  The guide
includes the following topics:

   * Introduction to MySQL functionality, MySQL Shell, and the 'world_x'
     example schema.

   * Operations to manage collections and documents.

   * Operations to manage relational tables.

   * Operations that apply to documents within tables.

To follow this quick-start guide you need a MySQL server with X Plugin
installed, the default in 8.0, and MySQL Shell to use as the client.
MySQL Shell includes X DevAPI, implemented in both JavaScript and
Python, which enables you to connect to the MySQL server instance using
X Protocol and use the server as a Document Store.

*Related Information*

   * MySQL Shell 8.0 (https://dev.mysql.com/doc/mysql-shell/8.0/en/)
     provides more in-depth information about MySQL Shell.

   * See Installing MySQL Shell
     (https://dev.mysql.com/doc/mysql-shell/8.0/en/mysql-shell-install.html)
     and *note x-plugin:: for more information about the tools used in
     this quick-start guide.

   * See Supported Languages
     (https://dev.mysql.com/doc/mysql-shell/8.0/en/mysql-shell-features.html#shell-supported-languages)
     for more information about the languages MySQL Shell supports.

   * X DevAPI User Guide
     (https://dev.mysql.com/doc/x-devapi-userguide/en/) provides more
     examples of using X DevAPI to develop applications which use MySQL
     as a Document Store.

   * A *note JavaScript: mysql-shell-tutorial-javascript. quick-start
     guide is also available.


