28.3.26 The INFORMATION_SCHEMA RESOURCE_GROUPS Table
----------------------------------------------------

The *note 'RESOURCE_GROUPS': information-schema-resource-groups-table.
table provides access to information about resource groups.  For general
discussion of the resource group capability, see *note
resource-groups::.

You can see information only for columns for which you have some
privilege.

The *note 'RESOURCE_GROUPS': information-schema-resource-groups-table.
table has these columns:

   * 'RESOURCE_GROUP_NAME'

     The name of the resource group.

   * 'RESOURCE_GROUP_TYPE'

     The resource group type, either 'SYSTEM' or 'USER'.

   * 'RESOURCE_GROUP_ENABLED'

     Whether the resource group is enabled (1) or disabled (0);

   * 'VCPU_IDS'

     The CPU affinity; that is, the set of virtual CPUs that the
     resource group can use.  The value is a list of comma-separated CPU
     numbers or ranges.

   * 'THREAD_PRIORITY'

     The priority for threads assigned to the resource group.  The
     priority ranges from -20 (highest priority) to 19 (lowest
     priority).  System resource groups have a priority that ranges from
     -20 to 0.  User resource groups have a priority that ranges from 0
     to 19.


