------------------------------------------------------------

The *note 'MYSQL_FIREWALL_WHITELIST':
information-schema-mysql-firewall-whitelist-table. table provides a view
into the in-memory data cache for MySQL Enterprise Firewall.  It lists
allowlist rules of registered firewall account profiles.  It is used in
conjunction with the 'mysql.firewall_whitelist' system table that
provides persistent storage of firewall data; see *note
firewall-tables::.

The *note 'MYSQL_FIREWALL_WHITELIST':
information-schema-mysql-firewall-whitelist-table. table has these
columns:

   * 'USERHOST'

     The account profile name.  Each account name has the format
     'USER_NAME@HOST_NAME'.

   * 'RULE'

     A normalized statement indicating an acceptable statement pattern
     for the profile.  A profile allowlist is the union of its rules.

As of MySQL 8.0.26, this table is deprecated and subject to removal in a
future MySQL version.  See *note firewall-account-profile-migration::.


